      "articleId": "e8b14da8d474cf6a5473",
      "headline": "Namibia pledges support for Eswatini's national research council",
      "dek": "Namibia committed to assisting Eswatini in establishing its National Research Council and strengthening its research, science, technology, and innovation system.",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Namibia has pledged continued support to Eswatini as the kingdom works to operationalize its National Research Council (NRC) and enhance its national research, science, technology, and innovation system. Dr. Nhlanhla Lupahla, General Manager for Research, Science, Technology and Innovation Coordination and Support at Namibia’s National Commission on Research, Science and Technology, stated that Namibia is ready to share its experiences and lessons with Eswatini.",
        "Lupahla emphasized that Namibia views the establishment of the council as a significant investment in Eswatini's capacity to use research, science, technology, and innovation to address national development priorities. He noted that the two countries share historical and regional ties, along with similar institutional environments, opportunities, and challenges in developing national research and innovation systems.",
        "Namibia's support will also extend to the continental science and research community, with Namibia planning to host the Science Granting Councils Initiative (SGCI) All Partners Meeting in Windhoek from September 27 to October 3, 2026. During this meeting, Namibia intends to support Eswatini's admission into the SGCI network, which would strengthen Eswatini's research ecosystem and contribute to the collective voice of science granting councils across Africa."
      ],
      "body": "Namibia has pledged continued support to Eswatini as the kingdom works to operationalize its National Research Council (NRC) and enhance its national research, science, technology, and innovation system. Dr. Nhlanhla Lupahla, General Manager for Research, Science, Technology and Innovation Coordination and Support at Namibia’s National Commission on Research, Science and Technology, stated that Namibia is ready to share its experiences and lessons with Eswatini.\n\nLupahla emphasized that Namibia views the establishment of the council as a significant investment in Eswatini's capacity to use research, science, technology, and innovation to address national development priorities. He noted that the two countries share historical and regional ties, along with similar institutional environments, opportunities, and challenges in developing national research and innovation systems.\n\nNamibia's support will also extend to the continental science and research community, with Namibia planning to host the Science Granting Councils Initiative (SGCI) All Partners Meeting in Windhoek from September 27 to October 3, 2026. During this meeting, Namibia intends to support Eswatini's admission into the SGCI network, which would strengthen Eswatini's research ecosystem and contribute to the collective voice of science granting councils across Africa.",
