      "body": "Niger's President, General Abdourahamane Tiani, called on parliamentarians from the Alliance of Sahel States (AES) to remain united to tackle the confederation's challenges. He received a delegation of presidents from the AES parliamentary bodies, led by Dr. Ousmane Bougouma, President of the Legislative Assembly of Burkina Faso, on August 25, 2026, in Niamey.\n\nDr. Bougouma stated that the delegation thanked President Tiani and the AES authorities for establishing the confederation's architecture, including the inaugural session and installation of confederal deputies. He noted that the AES Parliament is now operational, with an internal regulation adopted and three working commissions formed: Defense and Security, Diplomacy, and Development.\n\nPresident Tiani reminded the parliamentarians of the context surrounding the AES's creation and urged them to remain pragmatic, work to address the populations' concerns, and foster fraternity within the AES to build a space of security, development, and well-being for their people.",
