      "body": "The United States has proposed extending the arms embargo currently limited to Sudan's Darfur region to the entire country, including drones and their components, to stem the flow of weapons fueling the conflict since April 2023. This initiative, presented at a UN Security Council session on Monday, aims to strengthen the monitoring capacity of the panel of experts responsible for sanctions.\n\nDenmark, the UK, and France have publicly supported the US proposal. Denmark's foreign minister, Lars Løkke Rasmussen, also called for the International Criminal Court's jurisdiction to be extended across Sudan. However, China, Russia, and Sudan's UN representative oppose the expansion, with Russia's Vasily A Nebenzya arguing it would harm the Sudanese army.\n\nMassad Boulos, the US president’s senior adviser for Arab and African affairs, told the Security Council that more than twelve countries are providing military support to the warring parties, prolonging the conflict and increasing civilian casualties. Sudan's army chief, Abdelfattah El Burhan, dismissed the potential impact of any additional sanctions on the country.",
