      "articleId": "ce37e6564496829309e6",
      "headline": "Lesotho Correctional Service faces court challenge over officer promotions",
      "dek": "A senior officer has filed a High Court application to overturn the April 2026 promotions of three colleagues, alleging they lack required academic qualifications.",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Assistant Superintendent (AS) Karele Poqa is challenging the promotions of Assistant Commissioner (AC) Neo Moramotse, Senior Superintendent (SSP) Ramaketekete Rasehloho, and Superintendent (Supt) Sidwell Mothea. Poqa claims these officers were promoted despite not meeting the academic qualifications outlined in the Lesotho Correctional Service (LCS) promotion guidelines.",
        "According to Poqa's court papers, the promotions process, initiated by LCS Acting Commissioner Matingoa Phamotse in February 2026, was procedurally flawed. Poqa alleges that the academic credentials of candidates were not verified, and the Senior Officers Appointment Board was improperly constituted, lacking a public officer nominated by the Minister of Public Service.",
        "Poqa specifically states that AC Moramotse and SSP Rasehloho did not possess the degrees required for their new ranks. He seeks to have the court demote the three officers to their previous ranks of Senior Superintendent, Superintendent, and Assistant Superintendent, respectively."
      ],
      "body": "Assistant Superintendent (AS) Karele Poqa is challenging the promotions of Assistant Commissioner (AC) Neo Moramotse, Senior Superintendent (SSP) Ramaketekete Rasehloho, and Superintendent (Supt) Sidwell Mothea. Poqa claims these officers were promoted despite not meeting the academic qualifications outlined in the Lesotho Correctional Service (LCS) promotion guidelines.\n\nAccording to Poqa's court papers, the promotions process, initiated by LCS Acting Commissioner Matingoa Phamotse in February 2026, was procedurally flawed. Poqa alleges that the academic credentials of candidates were not verified, and the Senior Officers Appointment Board was improperly constituted, lacking a public officer nominated by the Minister of Public Service.\n\nPoqa specifically states that AC Moramotse and SSP Rasehloho did not possess the degrees required for their new ranks. He seeks to have the court demote the three officers to their previous ranks of Senior Superintendent, Superintendent, and Assistant Superintendent, respectively.",
